Run the touch thread on an A55 (sweet_amp_bind_little in the cpufreq driver).
The NT36672A is read over bit-banged I2C: ~6 ms of CPU per frame, a frame every ~8 ms while a finger is down, at kernel
priority 81. With 0256 every unbound thread runs on the A75s, so while the screen was touched the touch thread
preempted CoreAnimation's render thread (pri 54) on the same four cores (user: "when I touch it UI really stutters, it
only runs fine when scrolling slowly", 2026-10-29). After its start-up delay the touch thread binds itself to the
highest-numbered A55, which runs nothing else while only the A75s are recommended (thread_select still runs bound
threads on a CPU that is not recommended).

diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_cpufreq.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_cpufreq.c
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_cpufreq.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_cpufreq.c
@@ -520,6 +520,31 @@
 	    "all CPUs recommended");
 }
 
+/*
+ * 0257: bind the calling kernel thread to the highest-numbered A55, which runs nothing else while only the A75s are
+ * recommended (a CPU that is not recommended still runs the threads bound to it: thread_select). For the touch
+ * thread: it reads the NT36672A over bit-banged I2C (~6 ms of CPU per frame, a frame every ~8 ms while a finger is
+ * down) at kernel priority 81, so on an A75 it preempted CoreAnimation's render thread (pri 54) whenever the screen
+ * was touched ("when I touch it UI really stutters", 2026-10-29). The binding takes effect at the caller's next block.
+ */
+extern processor_t thread_bind(processor_t processor);   /* osfmk/kern/sched_prim.h, MACH_KERNEL_PRIVATE */
+void sweet_amp_bind_little(const char *who);
+void
+sweet_amp_bind_little(const char *who)
+{
+	if (cf_amp_little == 0) {
+		printf("SWEET AMP: %s stays unbound (no A55 mask)\n", who);
+		return;
+	}
+	int cpu = 63 - __builtin_clzll(cf_amp_little);
+	processor_t p = cpu_to_processor(cpu);
+	if (p == NULL) {
+		return;
+	}
+	(void)thread_bind(p);
+	printf("SWEET AMP: %s bound to CPU %d (A55)\n", who, cpu);
+}
+
 /* Core-class steering of the scheduler's idle-CPU choice (osfmk/kern/sched_prim.c). */
 static void
 cf_amp_setup(void)
diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
